RJ45 - 8P8C ETHERNET COLOR CODE
TIA/EIA-568  |  Twisted-pair LAN cable  |  8 positions, 8 contacts

STANDARDS
T568B  most common in new installs, commercial, consumer gear
T568A  older / some government / residential specs
Use the SAME standard on both ends = straight-through cable
Mix A and B = crossover (rarely needed on modern auto-MDI-X ports)

PIN ORDER  (front view, clip DOWN, contacts facing you, left-to-right)
Pin  1  2  3  4  5  6  7  8

T568B
1  White/Orange     Tx+   (Pair 2)
2  Orange           Tx-
3  White/Green      Rx+   (Pair 3)
4  Blue             Bi+   (Pair 1)   unused 10/100  |  used Gigabit + PoE
5  White/Blue       Bi-
6  Green            Rx-
7  White/Brown      Bi+   (Pair 4)   unused 10/100  |  used Gigabit + PoE
8  Brown            Bi-

T568A  (orange and green pairs swapped)
1  White/Green      Tx+   (Pair 3)
2  Green            Tx-
3  White/Orange     Rx+   (Pair 2)
4  Blue             Bi+   (Pair 1)
5  White/Blue       Bi-
6  Orange           Rx-
7  White/Brown      Bi+   (Pair 4)
8  Brown            Bi-

PAIRS (keep twists as close to the connector as possible)
Pair 1  Blue / White-Blue
Pair 2  Orange / White-Orange
Pair 3  Green / White-Green
Pair 4  Brown / White-Brown

SPEED NOTES
10/100BASE-T   uses only pins 1,2,3,6
1000BASE-T     uses all 8 pins (all 4 pairs bidirectional)
PoE            typically rides unused pairs or all pairs depending on mode

RULE
Match colors on both ends for a straight cable.
Never mix A and B unless you deliberately want a crossover.
